# Step 7 — Capture state

Three separate files. Each has its own update rule.

## 7a — `last_brief.md` (rolling daily state — overwrite each run)

Save `{{MEMORY_DIR}}/last_brief.md` with:
- Send timestamp
- Fires flagged (for tracking resolution tomorrow)
- Slipped items (for next-day search)
- Priority threads with draft status
- Team commitment statuses ({{DIRECT_REPORT_1}} + {{DIRECT_REPORT_2}})
- Key {{PRODUCT_NAME}} signals
- Upcoming deadlines

End with a single line: `*(Jira state → see jira_state.md | Fire calibrations → see calibrations.md)*`

## 7b — `jira_state.md` (persistent ledger — update in place, never fully overwrite)

File: `{{MEMORY_DIR}}/jira_state.md`

Update rules each run:
- **Promote**: if a "Suggested to create" ticket has Slack/Granola signals of active work → move it to "In Progress."
- **Complete**: if an "In Progress" ticket has signals of done → move to "Done."
- **Drop**: items in "Done" from the *previous* brief → remove them (they've been seen once).
- **Add**: new tickets to "Suggested to create" based on this brief's signals.
- **IDs**: if a Jira ID (e.g., EA-1234) appears in Slack or Granola → add to "Known ticket IDs."
- **Never** re-suggest creating a ticket already in the ledger.

Ledger format:
```
## Suggested to create (assume created — watch for In Progress/Done signals)
- {ticket title} — suggested {date}

## In Progress (watch for Done signals)
- {ticket title} — moved In Progress {date}

## Done (drop after next brief)
- {ticket title} — closed {date}

## Known ticket IDs (from Slack/Granola mentions)
- {EA-XXXXX} — {description}
```

## 7c — `calibrations.md` (permanent, append-only — never overwrite, only add)

File: `{{MEMORY_DIR}}/calibrations.md`

Only write to this file if explicit calibration feedback was given during this run (in chat, Slack reply, or 🚫 react). Append the new rule under `## Active calibrations` in this format:
```
- [{date}] NOT A FIRE: {pattern}
  Rule: {what Alfred should do instead}
  Source: {how this was signaled}
```
If no new calibrations this run, do not touch this file.

## 7d — Run log (prepend entry to `{{HOME_DIR}}/alfred-run-log.md`)

Prepend a new entry at the top of the log (below the header, above the previous entry). Keep it tight — this is a machine-readable audit trail.

Format:
```
## {YYYY-MM-DD} ~{HH:MM} AM/PM ET

**Fires:** {count}
{- one line per fire title}

**Resolved since last brief:** {count}
{- one line per resolved item}

**Drafts created:** {count}
{- channel or person name per draft}

**Jira movements:**
{- → Suggested to create: {titles}}
{- → In Progress: {titles}}
{- → Done: {titles}}
{(omit any subsection with no movements)}

**Data sources:** {source} ✅/⚠️/❌ · ...

**Days to rollout:** {n}
```

## 7e — Git backup (sync renderer code to repo only)

After the run log is written, sync only the renderer files back to the repo. Never commit memory files or installed SKILL.md files — they contain personal data.

```bash
cp "{{BRIEFS_DIR}}/alfred-build.py" "{{REPO_DIR}}/renderer/"
cp "{{BRIEFS_DIR}}/alfred-template.html" "{{REPO_DIR}}/renderer/"
cd "{{REPO_DIR}}" && git add renderer/ && git commit -m "Alfred brief {YYYY-MM-DD}" 2>/dev/null || true
```

The `|| true` means if push fails (no network), the brief still completes — never block on git.

# Step 8 — Fire macOS notification

After the HTML is open and state is saved, fire a notification summarizing the brief. This is the push signal that tells you the brief is ready — the HTML is the reading experience.

**Compose the notification body** as: `{fire_count} fire(s) · {days_remaining} days to rollout · {top_fire_one_liner}`

**Fire via Bash** (runs in background so it doesn't block):
```
osascript << 'EOF' &
set result to display alert "Alfred — Morning Brief is ready" message "{body}" buttons {"Dismiss", "Open Brief"} default button "Open Brief"
if button returned of result is "Open Brief" then
    do shell script "open '{{BRIEFS_DIR}}/alfred-brief-{YYYY-MM-DD}.html'"
end if
EOF
```

Replace `{body}` with the actual composed string and `{YYYY-MM-DD}` with today's date. If osascript fails for any reason, log and continue — the HTML is already open.


# Rules (recap)
- No moralizing. Practical, dense.
- No greetings/filler.
- Preserve Granola citation links.
- Honor "not a fire" calibrations.
- Email: DRAFT-ONLY. Create Gmail drafts for priority unresponded emails. NEVER send.
- Slack: DRAFT-ONLY for replies. Do NOT send a Slack DM of the brief. The HTML is the brief.
- Calendar: max 4 individuals, no distros, no C-suite.
- No audio generation.
